#X text 20 20 FLOURISH PROBE -- two ways to make one 404 pad stutter slower and slower while its pitch falls \, both retriggering on the 404. The rules are flourish.lua beside this file. Not part of Cut It: a menu patch in /sdcard/Patches/! debug/ \, and loading it stops the instrument until Cut It is selected again., f 120;
#X text 20 1000 KEYS (white \, from the lowest C) \, every one on pad A11: C retrigger \, the first hit A11 and the rest on chromatic ch 16 falling 48 to 36. D retrigger A11 at its own pitch. E DJFX Looper loaded on BUS 3 \, A11 once \, the loop on 10 ms later with SPEED falling. F the same with the loop on 230 ms later. G A11 once. A stop: the loop and the effect off \, SPEED back to normal., f 120;
#X text 20 1080 KNOBS: 1 run length 1 to 6 s. 2 first gap 10 to 150 ms \, and the loop's LENGTH. 3 last gap 80 to 800 ms. 4 the looper's final SPEED 5 to 100 percent. The looper goes on the 404's channel 3 (BUS 3 \, a master bus \, so it catches A11 whatever its bus): CC 83 picks the effect \, CC 19 switches it \, CC 16 to 18 are LENGTH \, SPEED and LOOP SW \, per the manual and a guess., f 120;
#X text 300 380 midiOutGate 0 and midiInGate 0 after mother's own push half a second in: mother echoes the keys to every port \, and the 404's pads would come back as keys (ref/module/boot.md)., f 34;
#X obj 1500 300 r~ inL;
#X obj 1500 350 throw~ outL;
#X obj 1650 300 r~ inR;
#X obj 1650 350 throw~ outR;
#X text 1500 400 The 404 is heard only through the Organelle: its outputs come in on inL and inR \, so the probe passes them through as Cut It does (C-4)., f 40;
